// choice.mn — a choice among options: `choose(options)` suspends the
// computation around it, and the handler that catches its resumptions says
// what choosing means. Search, backtracking and speculation are handlers over
// this one perform, never a second mechanism (PLAN §4④): `every` resumes once
// per option and joins what each answered, `first` resumes in order until an
// option answers something, and the compiler's own forking handlers bracket
// each resumption on the graph's trail.
effect Choice {
  choose(options: [a]) -> a
}

// Every option's answers, in the options' order: the body answers a list, and
// each resumption's list joins the install's.
handler every {
  choose(options) => options |> flat_map({ o => resume(o) }),
}

// The first option whose answer is something: the options are resumed in
// order until one answers `Some`, and none after it is resumed.
handler first {
  choose(options) => {
    fn try_option(found, o) = match found {
      None => resume(o),
      Some(_) => found,
    }
    options |> fold(None, try_option)
  },
}
